  "author": "whirligig",
  "version": "1",
  "notes": "The same 1.2 m trainer airframe with a 6.5 cc glow engine on the nose instead of a brushless motor, swinging an 11x6 propeller off a 220 g tank of methanol. It is here because a piston engine feels nothing like an electric motor and the model should show why: the engine makes its torque in a band and has none at all below idle, where a brushless motor makes its best torque standing still; it gets LIGHTER as it flies, moving the centre of gravity as the tank empties behind the firewall; and it is thirsty \u2014 about a litre an hour, which is why the tank is a fifth of the airframe weight and buys only twelve minutes. Datum is the wing quarter chord.",
